// SOUNDNESS QUEUE row boxdyn_mutborrow_arg_no_vtable (tier 4, `diag`). An ILLEGAL program is refused with a BACKEND internal error:
// passing `&mut b` for a `&mut dyn Sp` parameter, where `b` is a `Box<dyn Sp>` local, fails in mlir-gen with
//
//   mlir_gen: internal: no vtable for '&dyn Sp' as '&dyn Sp' — the fat pointer's vtable half would be left uninitialised …
//
// compile rc 1, no object file, no `error:` line.
//
// RECLASSIFIED 2026-09-15f-rustcaudit from tier 3 `refuses`: the row said "legal — `&mut Box<dyn Sp>` deref-coerces to `&mut dyn Sp`", a READING.
// legality: rustc 1.98.1 --edition 2024 on the twin src/compiler/probes/2026-09-15f-rustcaudit/rust/boxdyn_mutborrow_arg_no_vtable.rs: REFUSED
//   error[E0277]: the trait bound `Box<dyn Sp>: Sp` is not satisfied — "required for the cast from `&mut Box<dyn Sp>` to `&mut dyn Sp`"
// A `&mut dyn` target makes the coercion an UNSIZE of `Box<dyn Sp>`, never a deref coercion. The verdict is right; the sentence is the defect (E0277).
// The legal spelling `use_mut(&mut *b)` meets the SAME internal error: row boxdyn_mut_explicit_deref_arg_no_vtable (tier 3).
// ⚠ FOR THE OWNER: the SHARED spelling `use_ref(&b)` is equally E0277 in rustc (twin src/compiler/probes/2026-09-15f-rustcaudit/rust/control/tier34/boxdyn_shared_borrow_arg.rs),
// and pass fixture tests/logos/pass/boxdyn_borrow_arg_keeps_box_drop asserts it compiles, under docs/spec/types.md `coerce.deref.box-struct-borrow`
// — a clause in neither divergence registry whose `&Box<dyn Trait>` -> `&dyn Trait` half is false about Rust. Reported, not edited.
package boxdyn_mutborrow_arg_no_vtable;
use logos.mem.boxed;

trait Sp { fn v(&self) -> i64; }
struct A { x: i64 }
impl Sp for A { fn v(&self) -> i64 { return self.x; } }

fn use_mut(r: &mut dyn Sp) -> i64 { return r.v(); }

fn main() -> i32 {
    let mut b: Box<dyn Sp> = box_new(A { x: 42i64 });
    if use_mut(&mut b) != 42i64 { return 3i32; }
    return 0i32;
}
